      {
        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "The root घृणुँ belongs to the tanadi class with svarita-it marking it ubhayapadi, so it takes both parasmaipada (घृणोति) and atmanepada (घृणुते) forms. Stripping the इत् मार्कर, the base root is घृण्, which with the class-u augment forms the present stem.\n\nI'm working through whether laghupadha guna should apply before the उ vikarana — since उ isn't शित्, it counts as ardhadhatuka, which would normally trigger guna of the penultimate ऋ, giving something like घर्णोति. But the attested, traditionally cited form is घृणोति without guna, similar to other tanadi roots like तृणु which shows both तृणोति and तर्णोति as optional forms per the Siddhanta Kaumudi. This suggests there's a vikalpa (optional) guna rule at play for certain tanadi roots like क्षिणु, तृणु, and others in this class, and I'm trying to recall the exact wording of that rule from the Kaumudi's treatment of tanadi roots.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<answer>घृणोति</answer>"
      }
